  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Black people are not authentic or are being replaced by white people",
  "description": "This stereotype is implied by the visual of a blonde wig on a mannequin head juxtaposed with the text 'we should respect blacks'. The wig is used as a symbol to suggest that Black people are not 'real' or are being impersonated by white people, which is a racially charged and offensive trope. This stereotype is part of a broader pattern of racial dehumanization and is often used to justify discrimination or hostility toward Black people.",
